=== HOOK_PORT ===
useSettings.ts already conformant:
  - imports AppSettings + GasPriceStatus from @/api/types (regenerated by prompt 0011)
  - all 22 request<T>() URLs use no /api/v1 prefix
  - all query params snake_case (vehicle_id, suspended, poll_interval, enabled)
  - VersionInfo.require_cookie_consent kept (Phase-46 / Prompt 70)
  - Local interfaces (AuthStatus, Vehicle, UserPreferenceLatest, DashboardLayoutsPayload,
    PollingConfig, CaptureStats, VersionInfo) are minimal subsets / extensions of the
    backend wire shape used by this hook only — no migration to api/types needed because
    PollingConfig in api/types lacks the [key:string] index signature that
    PollingConfigPanel callers iterate dynamically (locked-policy continuation precedent
    from Phase-43/0023..0033 hook-type drift handling).
=== PAGE_PORT ===
features/settings is a configuration / preferences UI, not a telemetry display.
  Pages: SettingsPage.tsx (1).
  Components: 18 production .tsx files under components/ (TeslaAccountSection,
    FeatureToggles, RegionSettings, ActiveOrdersSection, GeneralSettings,
    GasPriceSettings, NotificationSettings, QuietHoursPanel, AppearanceSettings,
    AdvancedSettings, SettingsSearch, TOTPEnrollmentSection, SettingsExportImport,
    WebhookChannelsSection, ActiveSessionsSection, ResetSection, PrivacySection,
    SettingField).
  Grep across the entire features/settings/ tree for
    useSettings.convertX / convertDistance / convertSpeed / convertTemp /
    convertPressure / convertEnergy / miles_to* / temp_c|f / speed_mph /
    battery_temp / inside_temp / outside_temp / charge_rate / distance_mi /
    range_km|mi / odometer
  finds NO SI-conversion call sites because the only "unit"-shaped fields in
  this feature are the user's display preferences themselves
  (unit_of_length / unit_of_temp / unit_of_pressure / preferred_range / locale /
   currency_symbol / decimal_precision / gas_efficiency_mpg / base_cost_per_kwh /
   gas_price_per_unit / tz_display_default / timezone_user / ui_density /
   chart_palette / time_format_default), which are themselves the preferences
   that drive convertXFromSI elsewhere — converting them would be circular.
  All field accesses use snake_case matching AppSettings in @/api/types.
  Same no-op-port outcome pattern as Phase-43/0024 telemetry, /0031 automations,
  /0032 notifications, /0033 admin.
